   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 1",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br><br></p><p><span>Peninsula School Board, District 5 (2013-Present);&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Candidate, Superintendent of Public Instruction (2024);&nbsp;Pierce County Charter Review Commission, District 7 (2016)</span></p><p><br><br><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br><br></p><p><span>United States Navy Officer (retired); Public Finance Banker; Defense Contractor</span></p><p><br><br><b>Education</b><br><br></p><p><span>SNHU, B.S. Organizational Leadership; Magna cum Laude</span></p><p><br><br><b>Community Service</b><br><br></p><p>Current: Board President, Greater Gig Harbor Foundation; VFW Post 2463; American Legion Post 262; Gig Harbor Rotary. <span>Previous: President, City Club of Tacoma; Vice President, Hilltop Business Association; Board Member, World Trade Center Tacoma; Regional Coordinator, Drug Education for Youth; Junior Achievement; Habitat for Humanity.</span><br><br><b>Statement</b><br><br></p><p>Olympia has lost focus. As a Navy veteran, public finance banker, and 13-year school board member, <em>I help lead one of Washington’s top 10% school districts. </em>We focus on literacy, math, school safety, responsible spending, and career, technical, and skilled-trades pathways.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Olympia should strengthen schools, </span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">not cut K-12 programs</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">, including Running Start and Transitional Kindergarten, while passing an income tax and diverting money from the police and firefighter pension fund. </span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Washingtonians deserve better</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">.&nbsp;I will bring balance, accountability, and common sense to Olympia, standing with parents, students, seniors, veterans, law enforcement, and working families. I respectfully ask for your vote.</span></p><p><br><br>",
